 ## Follow-ups
 
 - `renderWidget` does not escape `w.id`, so an id with a quote breaks the markup. `src/render.ts:3`. Source: `widget-shell` .omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-shell/f2/trailer-implementation-audit.txt, note 1
+- `get` keys entries by widget id only, so a widget whose props changed still renders its old HTML after an edit. `src/cache.ts:12`. Source: `widget-cache` .omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache/f2/trailer-strategic-risk-review.txt, B1
+- `set` never evicts, so the cache grows without bound in a long-running dashboard. `src/cache.ts:40`. Source: `widget-cache` .omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache/f2/trailer-implementation-audit.txt, note 1
+- `set` takes `storedAt` before rendering, so an entry looks older than its HTML and any later age check would expire it early. `src/cache.ts:40`. Source: `widget-cache` .omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache/f2/trailer-implementation-audit.txt, note 2
+- `set` never evicts, so the cache grows without bound in a long-running dashboard. `src/cache.ts:40`. Source: `widget-cache` .omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache/f2/trailer-strategic-risk-review.txt, note 1
+- The cache and `renderWidget` both build the widget wrapper markup, so a markup change has to be made twice. `src/render.ts:3`. Source: `widget-cache` .omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache/f3-integration-review-report.md, note 1
